    "caveats": [
      "All monetary amounts (invoice.Total, invoiceline.UnitPrice, and track.UnitPrice) are already expressed in USD; do not apply a cents-to-dollars conversion.",
      "Use invoice.Total for invoice-level revenue. Joining invoice to invoiceline repeats each invoice header once per line, so SUM(invoice.Total) after that join will overstate revenue unless invoices are deduplicated or aggregation is performed before the join.",
      "Line Item Revenue (SUM(invoiceline.UnitPrice * invoiceline.Quantity)) is the correct sales measure when analyzing purchased tracks, genres, albums, or artists. It may be subject to normal floating-point precision differences from invoice totals.",
      "Invoice lines are at purchased-track grain. Quantity is currently always 1 in this data, but revenue logic should still multiply UnitPrice by Quantity.",
      "track.UnitPrice is the catalog list price, whereas invoiceline.UnitPrice is the price actually charged on a purchase; use the latter for realized sales.",
      "playlisttrack is a many-to-many bridge: tracks can belong to multiple playlists. Joining it to sales multiplies sales by playlist membership unless the query deliberately analyzes sales by playlist or deduplicates at the intended grain.",
      "Track-to-album-to-artist joins are many-to-one from tracks and invoice lines, suitable for attributing line-item revenue to albums and artists. Album and artist counts should use DISTINCT identifiers when joined to tracks or sales.",
      "employee.ReportsTo is a nullable self-reference to employee.EmployeeId; the top-level employee has no manager. Alias employee separately for employee versus manager queries.",
      "Customer location and invoice billing location are distinct snapshots/attributes. Use invoice BillingCountry/City for where an invoice was billed and customer Country/City for the customer profile.",
      "Company, customer State, invoice BillingState, and several contact fields are frequently nullable. Composer is also nullable for a material share of tracks.",
      "Invoice dates span 2009-01-01 through 2013-12-22; trend analyses are limited to this observed period."
    ],
